-- Art and architecture styles get a branch of the topic tree, culture.styles,
-- taken from the Getty Art & Architecture Thesaurus (AAT, Getty Research
-- Institute, ODC-By 1.0) instead of hand-made labels, the way the economy
-- branch is JEL. Source: the AAT Styles and Periods facet, its European
-- styles (Medieval, Renaissance-Baroque, modern European, Early
-- Christian-Byzantine) and international post-1945 styles and movements,
-- fetched from vocab.getty.edu/sparql. AAT's own broader-preferred hierarchy
-- is the ltree path, with its European / post-1945 wrappers dropped, so
-- 'culture.styles.post_1945_architecture_design' @> its Brutalism leaf. AAT's
-- regional groupings of peoples and cultures are left out, and so are
-- concepts whose note describes a people rather than a style.
--
-- A topic is named by AAT's English preferred label without its
-- disambiguating parenthesis, in its -ism form when AAT has that as an
-- alternative label (Brutalist -> Brutalism); a guide term (<...>) keeps its
-- wording. Its description is AAT's scope note, then its other English labels,
-- then its AAT id. aat_id names a topic's AAT concept.
alter table public.topics
  add column aat_id text check (aat_id ~ '^3[0-9]{8}$');

on conflict (id) do update
  set name = excluded.name, description = excluded.description, aat_id = excluded.aat_id;

on conflict (id) do update
  set name = excluded.name, description = excluded.description, aat_id = excluded.aat_id;
